{"from": "text:josephus-war-6-house-doomed", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:mt-23-37-38-jerusalem-desolate", "grade": "B", "note": "Josephus (War 6.249-250) records that the Temple, the 'house', was burned on the tenth of Lous in 70 CE. It attests that the later desolation happened, not that it was predicted; graded B rather than A because 'left desolate' in 23:38 may mean abandonment rather than destruction. Edge added by the architect: the runner reported this find, but the edge was missing."}
